ly  gives um you know the quarterback  confidence but it gives everybody else  confidence when you see a receiver  coming with a 50 50 ball i feel like  that gives you momentum and energy  throughout the whole team and if we  could create more of those situations  and myself included setting that tone  then i feel like we're going to have a  really strong year as a wide receiver  group  look what are some of your specific  goals like are you a guy that comes into  the season that says hey i want to be  all pro i want to be a pro bowler i want  to catch a hundred passes do you have  those type of goals or do you just say  hey i'm just going to work and whatever  my team needs me to do i'm just gonna do  i think it's more so of that um i try  not to get too wrapped up in the  statistical part of the game obviously  we're judged off of a production so i  obviously want to be as productive as  possible but um you know i don't really  come into the season like i need this  many catches of this many yards this  many touchdowns i just need to be able  to do whatever my team calls me to do um  you know some games it'll be more so in  the run game some games it'll be i have  to take the load and catch eight to ten  passes i mean i feel like i'm the type  of player where i'm i have the  versatility to be able to do whatever  i'm asked to do it's just a matter of  being consistent weekend and week out  and getting stronger as the season  progresses and when you when they need  me most that's when i come down with  those plays so that's the type of  pressure i put on myself that's the type  of expectation i have for myself so um i  feel like my teammates feel that and um  i'm just continually trying to work so i  can continue to gain their trust and  continue to have that you know that um  that that relationship with fitz or  wherever the quarterback is um where  they could trust that 17 is going to be  open  yeah speaking of which you've you know  as a receiver dealing with so