w they how  they play off him but another guy i feel  like  um i like a lot is i like mike evans  game you know people don't really  necessarily necessarily notice how well  he he could get behind guys like he  could really stretch the field for being  as big as he is  he's strong at the point of catch like  um so i really respect the way he plays  the game and he's a dude who don't  really get a lot of coverage but he  don't really talk a lot either you know  what i mean like some guys cry because  they don't really get that recognition  or that that um that attention that  other guys get but he just puts his head  down and he works so i respect him for  that and um but like i said i got a lot  of respect for a lot of the receivers in  this league and it's cool to be a part  of such a fun group of guys um you know  trying to take this position to the next  level  last question with with all these young  wide receivers getting drafted what  advice would you give them because  you're you're a young man that has a  great head on his shoulders i mean  you've been productive you never  complain you try to do all the right  things but what advice would you give a  lot of these young wide receivers coming  to the  league um first of all i think i'd  probably say um first thing you're  coming in whether you're a first round  pick or you're an undrafted guy come in  and know what you're doing i feel like i  shared was one that you care and two is  only going to help you out because you  know when i came in as a third round guy  and kind of expected to play special  teams or whatever i wanted to make sure  i may have got three or four reps of  practice you know i mean but i was going  to make sure those reps was  100  i knew what i was doing i was right  where i needed to be and i was going to  make the play i feel like that that goes  a long way from just not just your  coaches but it builds your confidence  because you're allowed you're able to  learn on the fly and adapt 